==== NAME
pdxping -- minimal ICMP echo CLI, the first exerciser of the
R_NET_PRIVILEGED_PROTOCOL elevate class.

==== SYNOPSIS
    pdxping [--count=N] [--interval-ms=N] [--timeout-ms=N] [--dry-run] <host>

Defaults: count=4, interval-ms=1000, timeout-ms=1000. `<host>` is
required; no default.

==== DESCRIPTION
`pdxping` is a standalone ring-3 ELF -- its own `_start`, no shared
library, no dynamic linker. It is deliberately small: one echo per
syscall, one blocking wait for the matching reply, no traceroute, no
MTU discovery, no flood mode (`design/networking/r100-user-tools-plan.md`
§5, paideia-os repo).

At v1.2.0, only the `--dry-run` path is reachable: `--count`
`PingRecord@0.1` records are built, each is emitted over the
semantic-pipe path (`sys_semantic_send`, sysno 115 -- WEAK stub, no-op
today) and audited (`libpdx-audit` -- WEAK stub, no-op today), then
its 128 raw bytes are previewed to fd 2 as a hex dump, one per
iteration, no network I/O. A non-`--dry-run` invocation calls the
`R_NET_PRIVILEGED_PROTOCOL` elevate gate before any echo attempt; the
gate is a fail-closed WEAK stub at this landing (no broker-endpoint
cap is provisioned to this tool), so every non-`--dry-run` invocation
exits 13 with `[pdxping.M3-001 EACCES]` on fd 2 -- even though this
repo now implements a real `--count` `sys_icmp_echo` (sysno 103) loop
with min/avg/max RTT + loss-percent summary stats (`src/icmp_wire.pdx`,
`src/entry.pdx`'s `ep_real_grant` arm), that loop is unreachable until
BOTH a real elevate-broker cap is provisioned to this tool AND the
kernel-side gate (`cap_check_r_net_privileged_protocol`, landed at
R100-PREP-003) opens to ordinary ring-3 callers, not just the
boot-witness/init context.

==== EXIT STATUS
    0   OK (--dry-run completed; every PingRecord@0.1 previewed)
    2   argv error (missing <host>, unknown flag, malformed numeric value)
    13  R_NET_PRIVILEGED_PROTOCOL elevate refused (fail-closed; every
        non---dry-run invocation at this landing)

==== LIMITATIONS
See CHANGELOG.md "Known deferred substrate": the real `--count` echo
loop, RTT/loss summary stats, `libpdx-elevate`, `libpdx-audit`, and
semantic-pipe emit are all implemented but remain WEAK stubs / dead
code pending a real cross-repo link path and a kernel-side gate
opening -- every non-`--dry-run` invocation exits 13 today.

M4 smoke coverage (`tests/pdxping_happy_smoke.pdx`,
`tests/pdxping_timeout_smoke.pdx`,
`tests/pdxping_elevate_denied_smoke.pdx`) exists as compile-only
pipeline-replay drivers -- each exports `run() -> u64`, is compiled by
`tools/build.sh`'s own `tests/*.pdx` glob to verify it assembles, but
none is linked or executed under real QEMU boot yet (see
`tests/README.md`).

